    "https://awslabs.github.io/duvet/v2/sources.json#inline": {
      "src-960281a3e276111b": {
        "file_name": "spec/rfc9999.txt",
        "contents": "\n\n\n\n\nInternet Engineering Task Force (IETF)                         A. Author\nRequest for Comments: 9999                                   Example Org\nCategory: Standards Track                                   October 2026\nISSN: 2070-1721\n\n\n                      Example Token Exchange Protocol\n\nAbstract\n\n   This document describes an example protocol for tests.\n\n1.  Introduction\n\n   This section has no requirement.\n\n2.  Requests\n\n   The client MUST send the token.\n\n   The server MUST reject invalid tokens.\n\n   The server SHOULD log the request.\n\n2.1.  Parameters\n\n   The server MUST validate the café parameter and the response\n   MUST be encoded as JSON.\n\n   The client MAY cache the response.\n\n3.  Security\n\n   Servers SHOULD rotate their keys.\n\n   The token MUST NOT be empty.\n\n   The server MUST reject replayed tokens and SHOULD alert the\n   administrator.\n\n   The server MUST:\n\n   o  reject expired tokens,\n\n   o  reject revoked tokens.\n"
      },
      "src-db74e075a778c87e": {
        "file_name": "spec/extension.md",
        "contents": "# Example extension\n\n## Discovery\n\nThe server SHOULD publish its \"metadata\".\n"
      }
    },
